From 536e7b0abca2d253599073a732e6e7f0c4f072b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:37:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): `kanban quota-release` ends a stale
 quota episode; the release is an episode boundary

During the 11-12 revoked-token outage every usable Claude account failed with 401, so worker
startup raised SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable with the reset of the accounts genuinely at 100%.
That hint became a hinted episode which decision() trusted until its deadline: 10+ ready cards
were held 1-6 days while anthropic had capacity again.

PR #1409 (18877042c6/7eaf64bd63/f0c7044430) landed the automatic path: _outstanding drops a
hinted wall the live OAuth pool disproves to its doubling backoff, and the reclaim phase prunes
disproved provider walls. This change, rebased onto it, keeps only what that path does not cover
(the auto-release half of the earlier head, _held/live_pool_capacity/admit, is dropped as
redundant with _disproved):

- `hermes kanban quota-release <id> [--reason]`: operator-only, home gateway. Appends a
  quota_episode_released event, clears the card's quota error stamp, comments QUOTA RELEASED.
- episode() treats quota_episode_released as a boundary: the released runs never form an
  episode again.
- The release clears the provider_walls.json entry copied from the released hint
  (record_wall only extends); a later wall stays (kanban_provider_walls.drop_wall).
- Queue note says "quota hold released (...)" until the next run; guard_hold_until no longer
  falls back to the old receipt reset after a release.

Card: t_01a1cfac4046a296
